      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T12:22:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your patience, this is a most interesting read as it shows the set of all the things a complete implementation needs to care about.\n\nOne structural thing to change is that the Render/ComputePipeline should explicitly know where each root constant used is located, and pass that explicitly to the HLSL compilation. Querying stuff after transforms is actually something that the Tint team wants to remove over time, it just hasn\u0027t done it for HLSL yet.\n\nSo RenderPipelineD3D12 would during initialization completely determine which root constants are needed and their offsets in the register space used for all root constants and pass that to TranslateHLSL. So I think a pre-CL for this would be to change the current Dawn to do that and stack the immediate CL on top (it allows landing that part without waiting for the rest of the design to stick).\n\nSo that\u0027s two pre-CLs that we can do:\n\n - Making Compute/RenderPipelineD3D12 push to HLSL compilation the register offset / space of the builtins and which builtins are used.\n - Landing immediateDataSize in PipelineLayout + limit, validation and validation tests.\n \nI\u0027m pretty convinced that we can have a small solution for handling root constants using dirty bits that would be faster and more ergonomic to use than a whole extra object. Though we\u0027ll have to be careful when to consider things dirty (for example a pipeline change should dirty all the bits used by the pipeline as a first approximation, but DispatchIndirect with NumWorkgroups set in the indirect commands shouldn\u0027t need to apply NumWorkgroups directly since we don\u0027t know what it is).\n\nLet me know if you\u0027d like a small meeting to discuss all of this, I know it\u0027s a lot but a clear solution is in sight!",
      "revId": "1392ccb155b29453b7f1c581eb4f814d7ca830c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
