      "writtenOn": "2024-09-09T16:51:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I need to think about this a bit more, but I think we could try to have a simpler data layout for this instead of reaching out in the pipeline all the time.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\n// Defined in pipeline layout.\nConstantIndex \u003d ityp::TypedInteger\u003cuint8_t, struct ConstnatIndexT\u003e;\n\n// Common constants\nConstantIndex immediateStart \u003d 0;\nConstnatIndex bufferLengthStart \u003d immediateStart + 4;\n\n// Constants for compute\nConstantIndex numWorkgroup \u003d bufferLengthStart + N;\nConstantIndex maxConstantComputes \u003d numWorkgroup + 3;\n\nstruct RootConstants\u003ccompute vs. render\u003e {\n   // Helpers to set dirty + values\n   SetNumWorkgroups(x, y, z);\n   SetBufferLength();\n   \n   ityp::bitset\u003cmaxofcompute vs render\u003e dirty;\n   std::array\u003cmaxofcompute vs render, uint32_t\u003e values;\n};\n\nRootConstants rootconstants;\n\nAt some point before draw:\n    // Aplpy missing constants\n    Get mask of used constants from the pipeline.\n    Or it with the dirty constants.\n    Somehow call setRootConstants correctly.\n    \nOf course dirtying also sometimes needs to happen when switching root signature or w/e.\n```\n\nSry for messy comment, I have to leave for something but wanted to get this in today.",
      "revId": "1392ccb155b29453b7f1c581eb4f814d7ca830c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
