      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T12:22:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Either a dirty bit or min-max works for the actual call to SetRootConstants, but for tracking I believe dirty bits are better because they allow easy masking with the pipeline\u0027s mask of used constants. The problem otherwise is that it becomes difficult to find that the min in the RootConstant in the stack variable is the actual min for the pipeline, or how to update it if the pipeline doesn\u0027t use that min variable.\n\nSo we can do min/max (using ScanForward / ScanBackward) or a few calls for `Somehow call setRootConstants correctly.`, but the tracking would still use dirty bits. WDYT?\n\n\u003e If we have new \"RootSignature\" object, I\u0027d like to put this immediate data block struct/class in RootSignatureBase.\n\nDeduplicating the code between backends would be nice, but I don\u0027t think that it is possible here because they all have their own special immediates to set for workaround / emulation. They also use different mechanisms to set them. D3D12 and Vulkan are similar but Metal would use setBytes, D3D11 a dynamic uniform buffer and GL just GL uniforms. So overall handling of immediate, both in the layout, the shader module and the command buffer would be per-backend. The frontend just says how many the user needs.",
      "parentUuid": "787f017f_6eb991e6",
      "revId": "1392ccb155b29453b7f1c581eb4f814d7ca830c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
