      "writtenOn": "2024-09-10T12:22:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ultimately the pipeline should be the one computing how many root constants it needs and what each one corresponds to but the root signature only depends on how many root constants are needed. So for example in the render pipeline initialization we\u0027d do:\n\n```\nConstantIndex mUsedConstants;\n// This could be in d3d12::PipelineBase\nmUsedConstants |\u003d constantsForImmediates (0, 0b1, 0b11, 0b111 or 0b1111, we\u0027d have a helper function doing bit twiddling for that).\nmUsedConstants |\u003d constantsForDynamicBuffers;\n\n// This could be in d3d12::RenderPipeline\nif (uses vertex index) { mUsedConstants |\u003d ConstantIndex::VertexIndex}\nif (uses instance index) { mUsedConstants |\u003d ConstantIndex::VertexIndex}\n\n// Equivalent in d3d12::ComputePipeline.\n\n\n// In PipelineBase?\nrootSignature \u003d layout-\u003eGetRootSignature(popcount(mUsedConstants))\n```",
      "revId": "1392ccb155b29453b7f1c581eb4f814d7ca830c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
